course: dictionary
lesson: 7438
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Polo is a good example. It can name a sport played on horses, a game in a swimming pool, a short shirt, or a high-necked jumper.
explain: Look at the words around it. If the text mentions horses, mallets and a goal, polo is the sport. If it mentions a short-sleeved shirt with a collar, polo is clothing. If it says «polo neck», it means a jumper.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. Try «The team wore white polo shirts» with the meaning jumper. Does it still make sense? No, so the clothing meaning that fits is the shirt.
fact: Polo can be a game played on horseback, using long-handled wooden mallets to hit a small ball into the other team's goal.
fact: Water polo is a team game played in a swimming pool, where swimmers throw a ball into a goal.
fact: A polo shirt is a short-sleeved cotton shirt with a collar and a few buttons at the neck.
fact: A polo neck is a jumper with a high, folded collar round the neck. In the USA it is called a turtleneck.
fact: Marco Polo is a name: a famous Italian traveller who went to China.
exercise: «The team played a polo match on horseback, hitting the ball with long mallets.» What does polo mean here? | A swimming race | A short-sleeved shirt | *A game played on horseback | A high-necked jumper
exercise: «She pulled on her warm black polo neck before going out in the snow.» What is a polo neck? | A short-sleeved cotton shirt | A swimming cap | A saddle for a horse | *A jumper with a high, folded collar
exercise: «The swimmers threw the ball into the goal across the pool.» Which kind of polo is this? | Polo on horseback | Polo shirt | *Water polo | Polo neck
test: «Dad wore a white polo shirt with three buttons at the neck.» What is a polo shirt? | A famous traveller | A jumper for snowy days | A tall wooden stick for hitting balls | *A short-sleeved cotton shirt with a collar
test: Marco Polo is a name, not a sport. Who was he? | *A famous Italian traveller to China | A famous English footballer | A goalkeeper in water polo | A horse rider from ancient Persia
exam: «On a cold morning, Sam pulled on his black polo neck and went out.» What is a polo neck? | Water polo | *A jumper with a high collar | Polo on horseback | A short-sleeved shirt
